@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `vn11-nouns`
IMPORT `vn11-art01-02-definitions`
IMPORT `vn11-art03-benefits`
IMPORT `vn11-art04-07-premiums`
IMPORT `vn11-art08-13-conditions`
IMPORT `vn11-art14-18-administration`

-- Manulife Vietnam term life product terms, row VN-11: a death claim, put together from the
-- Articles. Three layers, kept apart:
--   1. was the contract in force on the day of the death, and does a limitation or exclusion bite?
--      (Arts 1.3, 1.5, 1.6, 3(c), 4, 5, 7, 9, 10, 11, 18)
--   2. how much is payable? (Arts 3(a), 3(b), 5, 8, 9)
--   3. what must be done, and by when? (Art 16: the time to claim, the evidence, the duty to pay)
-- No new source text is encoded here, so no new src: lines are quoted; each limb cites its Article.
--
-- The order of the arms of `the outcome of the death claim` is a reading (fork F18): the questions
-- the document answers for every contract (the term, cancellation, lapse) come before the ones it
-- answers for some (Arts 9, 10, 11, 3(c)), and the claim's time bar is applied to the death benefit
-- only, not to the premium refunds of Arts 3(c), 9 and 11. Where the document is silent the answer
-- is a named refusal from the Article's own module (Arts 1.3, 1.5, 5, 7).

§ `A death claim`

§§ `Layer 1 — the contract on the day of the death`

GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day of death in` `the case` MEANS
    `the case`'s `death`'s `date of death`

@ref Art 1.6, src:54-56
GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the death fell in the contract term` `the case` MEANS
    `Art 1.6 — the day falls in the contract term` (`the case`'s `contract page`) (`the day of death in` `the case`)

-- A request sent in time on or before the day of the death cancels the contract under Art 4; the
-- document does not deal with a request sent after the death (fork F12).
@ref Art 4, src:185-188
GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the contract had been cancelled under Art 4 by the day of the death` `the case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the case`'s `requests`'s `date a written request to cancel was sent`
    WHEN NOTHING        THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST `the day` THEN
            `the day` AT MOST `the day of death in` `the case`
        AND `Art 4 — a request sent on` `the day` `is in time for a contract received on` (`the case`'s `requests`'s `date the contract was received`)

@ref Art 5, src:155-161; Art 18(i), src:403-404
GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the contract had lapsed under Art 5 by the day of the death` `the case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the case`'s `premiums`'s `instalment in default`
    WHEN NOTHING                THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST `the instalment` THEN `Art 5 — the contract had lapsed by` (`the day of death in` `the case`) `for non-payment of` `the instalment`

-- A death on the day of the request is read as still covered (fork F15).
@ref Art 18(iv), src:407-408
GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the policyholder had ended the contract before the day of the death` `the case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the case`'s `requests`'s `date the policyholder requested termination`
    WHEN NOTHING        THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST `the day` THEN `the day` LESS THAN `the day of death in` `the case`

@ref Art 10, src:257-276
GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Company has validly treated the contract as void under Art 10` `the case` MEANS
        `the case`'s `disclosure`'s `the Company has treated the contract as void under Art 10`
    AND `Art 10 — the Company may treat the contract as void` (`the case`'s `disclosure`) (`the case`'s `contract page`) (`the case`'s `premiums`) (`the day of death in` `the case`)

@ref Art 1.3, src:28-31
GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Age at issue in` `the case` MEANS
    `the Age of` (`the case`'s `insured`) `on` (`the case`'s `contract page`'s `issue date`)

§§ `Layer 2 — how much`

@ref Art 9, src:237-248
GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Age or sex misstated in` `the case` MEANS
        `the case`'s `application`'s `Age misstated in it`
    OR  `the case`'s `application`'s `sex misstated in it`

@ref Art 3(a)(i), src:83-85; Art 9, src:237-248
GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum insured, as corrected under Art 9, in` `the case` MEANS
    IF   `Age or sex misstated in` `the case`
    THEN `Art 9 — the sum insured after the misstatement is corrected` (`the case`'s `contract page`'s `sum insured`) (`the case`'s `premiums`'s `total premium paid`) (`the case`'s `premiums`'s `total premium payable at the true Age and sex`)
    ELSE `the case`'s `contract page`'s `sum insured`

@ref Art 1.4, src:32-33; Art 3(b), src:101-103
GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Age at death in` `the case` MEANS
    `the Age of` (`the case`'s `insured`) `on` (`the day of death in` `the case`)

@ref Art 3(a), src:76-93; Art 3(b), src:94-126; Art 5, src:162-169
GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the death benefit under Art 3 in` `the case` MEANS
    `Art 3(a) — the death benefit`
        (`the sum insured, as corrected under Art 9, in` `the case`)
        (`the Age at death in` `the case`)
        (`the case`'s `claim`'s `rider benefits payable`)
        (`Art 5 — the premiums deducted from the death benefit as unpaid` (`the case`'s `premiums`))

@ref Art 3(c), src:171-173; Art 9, src:252-254; Art 11, src:282-284
GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the premium refunded in` `the case` MEANS
    `the premium refunded, without interest, after the reasonable costs` (`the case`'s `premiums`'s `total premium paid`) (`the case`'s `premiums`'s `reasonable costs and expenses deducted by the Company`)

@ref Art 9, src:242-244
GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the excess premium refunded under Art 9 in` `the case` MEANS
    IF   `Age or sex misstated in` `the case`
    THEN `Art 9 — the excess premium refunded, without interest` (`the case`'s `premiums`'s `total premium paid`) (`the case`'s `premiums`'s `total premium payable at the true Age and sex`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `The outcome`

@ref Arts 1.3, 1.5, 1.6, 3, 4, 5, 7, 9, 10, 11, 16, 18
GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A `The outcome of a death claim`
`the outcome of the death claim` `the case` MEANS
  BRANCH
    IF NOT `the death fell in the contract term` `the case`
        THEN `no death benefit: the contract was not in force` "Art 1.6: the death fell outside the contract term"
    IF NOT `the case`'s `premiums`'s `first premium paid`
        THEN `Art 5 does not say whether the contract is in force before the first premium is paid`
    IF `the contract had been cancelled under Art 4 by the day of the death` `the case`
        THEN `no death benefit: the contract was not in force` "Art 4: the policyholder had cancelled the contract"
    IF `the contract had lapsed under Art 5 by the day of the death` `the case`
        THEN `no death benefit: the contract was not in force` "Arts 5 and 18(i): the contract had lapsed at the end of the grace period"
    IF `the policyholder had ended the contract before the day of the death` `the case`
        THEN `no death benefit: the contract was not in force` "Art 18(iv): the policyholder had ended the contract"
    IF `the Company has validly treated the contract as void under Art 10` `the case`
        THEN `the Company has treated the contract as void`
    IF `Art 9 — a misstated Age, and the true Age at issue outside Art 1.3` (`the case`'s `application`) (`the case`'s `insured`) (`the case`'s `contract page`)
        THEN `no death benefit, and the premium is refunded` "Art 9" (`the premium refunded in` `the case`)
    IF NOT `Art 1.5 — the application is valid` (`the case`'s `application`)
        THEN `Art 1.5 does not say what follows when the application was not signed by both the policyholder and the insured`
    IF NOT `Art 7 — the insured resided in Vietnam on the day the contract was issued` (`the case`'s `insured`)
        THEN `Arts 1.3 and 7 do not say what follows when the insured did not reside in Vietnam on the issue date`
    IF NOT `Art 1.3 — an Age from 0 to 60` (`the Age at issue in` `the case`)
        THEN `Art 1.3 does not say what follows when the contract was issued at an Age outside 0 to 60 that was not misstated`
    IF `Art 11 — a suicide within 2 years of the issue date or of a reinstatement` (`the case`'s `death`) (`the case`'s `contract page`) (`the case`'s `premiums`)
        THEN `no death benefit, and the premium is refunded` "Art 11" (`the premium refunded in` `the case`)
    IF `Art 3(c) — the death benefit is excluded for` (`the case`'s `death`)
        THEN `no death benefit, and the premium is refunded` "Art 3(c)" (`the premium refunded in` `the case`)
    IF NOT `Art 16 — the claim was made in time` (`the case`'s `death`) (`the case`'s `claim`)
        THEN `the claim for the death benefit is out of time`
    OTHERWISE `the death benefit is payable` (`the death benefit under Art 3 in` `the case`)

§§ `Layer 3 — the beneficiaries, settlement, and the Company's duty to pay`

@ref Art 3(a), Art 8, src:222-227
GIVEN `the case`          IS A `A death claim`
      `the beneficiaries` IS A LIST OF `A beneficiary designation`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the amounts paid to the beneficiaries in` `the case` `the beneficiaries` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the outcome of the death claim` `the case`
    WHEN `the death benefit is payable` `the amount` THEN `Art 8 — the amounts paid to the beneficiaries, in the order they are named` `the beneficiaries` `the amount`
    OTHERWISE map (GIVEN b YIELD 0) `the beneficiaries`

@ref Art 16, src:337-362
GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Company must now settle the death benefit in` `the case` MEANS
        `a death benefit is payable`
    AND `Art 16 — the Company has received the evidence it requires` (`the case`'s `claim`)
    WHERE
        `a death benefit is payable` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the outcome of the death claim` `the case`
            WHEN `the death benefit is payable` `the amount` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The duty to pay, counted in calendar days from the day the claim was made (AT 0 in a #TRACE).
@ref Art 16, src:376-383
GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act`
`the Company's duty to pay the death benefit in` `the case` MEANS
    IF   `the Company must now settle the death benefit in` `the case`
    THEN `Art 16 — the Company must pay the death benefit, with interest once two months have passed` (`Art 16 — the days in the two months after the claim` (`the case`'s `claim`))
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref Art 18, src:400-409
GIVEN `the case` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A `A termination under Art 18`
`the termination of the contract in` `the case` MEANS
    `Art 18 — the termination of the contract` (`the case`'s `contract page`) (`the case`'s `premiums`) (`the case`'s `requests`) (JUST (`the day of death in` `the case`))
